we have been waiting for apple to bring  back touch id for years now and some  people even are saying that they will  not upgrade to a new iphone until apple  does so and it seems like apple is  listening because they're still filing  patents creating new technology with one  patent that was still updated just  yesterday but with that said even though  we have people like mark german and ming  chi ko saying that this is going to be  coming out a new under display  technology i believe that this will  never happen and we will never have  under display touch id on any iphone and  i'll explain exactly why believe it or  not apple has been working on this under  display tech since 2013  when they filed this patent that was  officially granted to them in  2015 and this shows an acoustic imaging  system that basically vibrates and  senses your fingerprint in order to  unlock it which is crazy now of course  this never came out but a couple years  after that they started making new  patents with new technology for the  iphone 10. this one used an optical  method with maybe a more accurate system  and they had this in the works for that  in order to be able to have a better  design without having that touch id  button but they ended up having issues  with not enough yield making this  possible with a company that they bought  a few years back and in the end we know  that face id ended up working out they  got it to work and then they no longer  had to rely on this or some of the  prototypes with the touch of the sensor  being on the back as basically plan c a  fail safe after that you would think  that apple would stop working on this  and just adopt face id completely but  they didn't they got another patent on  another technology that could make this  possible and use the display to read  your fingerprint and with that we kept  getting rumors of new iphones coming out  with this and i'll just fast forward and  say that iphone 13  was tested to have under display touch  id with five different analysts leaking  info with supply chain leaks showing  that this is what's gonna happen but of  course we know that it did not and the  iphone 13 did not adopt this technology  and the weird thing is these guys are  still talking about apple working on  under display touch id for the iphone 14  now but like i said i don't think that  this is going to happen and i believe  there are three reasons why it won't now  the first one is because this keeps  getting delayed and delayed the leaks  and the rumors and of course it is fun  but after you go from year to year and  it keeps getting pushed back it is just  annoying like i said uh first is gonna  come for the iphone 13 we had all the  info supply chain and then we see  updates for it coming for the iphone 14  and 2022 so that is this year but now we  have the latest release and it is  getting pushed back to 2023  and as we go on tech gets better  and this is where the second reason  comes in and that's the fact that face  id itself is getting better we know that  apple is updating the iphone design with  the hole punch camera that the  technology that allows face id to work  is getting smaller they're working on it  working underneath the display as well  and once they reach that do they need to  have an underneath the display face id  and touch id at the same time i don't  think so i think the final goal was to  achieve face id underneath the display  or at least not have that huge notch and  i don't think that they expected it to  take this long for underneath the  display touch id to properly  work and with that we also know that  apple wants to implement face id across  their lineup it's now included in ipads  and we also know that in the coming  years they are going to add it to more  ipads as well  and the same thing goes with macbooks  and potentially imacs we've had leaks  rumors uh and basically hardware info  that is going to be coming out we want  an imax we know that these new macbooks  have this notch even though the actual  camera portion of it is really tiny  apple left that extra space  for them to be able to put face id into  the macbook now i wish they did out of  the get-go maybe they're just waiting  for the smaller tech to be able to work  so that they won't need as much  thickness and it can work in the shape  but it's quite obvious that apple's  moving forward with that and of course  it's going to be great to have that with  your imax and ipads and everything else  now the final reason why i don't think  that the under display  touch id is ever going to come is  because of what they just released and  that is the latest version of ios they  release the ability to finally use face  id with a mask now this part of it just  blows my mind and this is the clear  reason that i think they're ditching  touch id  we've had this situation with a pandemic  and with masks for almost two years now  and people have been complaining this  about this this has been their biggest  complaint is just that so inconvenient  to use now sure if you think about it we  could give apple a pass for maybe a few  months maybe even half a year but it's  been almost two years and they just  released this software fix to be able to  allow you to do this now my thought is  they were working on this underneath the  display fingerprint tech we know there's  new patents that were filed in 2020 as  well to get the latest version to work  they're successful uh they have parts  it's super accurate now as well way more  accurate than before and we know that  even in january apple was working on  that for the iphone 13  that way they could capitalize on this  issue and give people another reason to  upgrade to the iphone 13. of course we  have the patents  but as we know it never happened and in  order for this to happen it not only has  to be able to work but it has to be  accurate enough in the fact that it's  going to be secure and also responsive  enough where it's going to work well  we know that with other under display  technologies for example we have one  plus that used that we have samsung  they had issues one plus we were able to  easily hack it in samsung's we did hack  but it was a lot more difficult but then  again samsung's it took a lot longer to  read it was less accurate there'd be a  lot of times it would fail and they've  been slowly improving on that technology  and for apple to adopt something it  needs to be good enough and it needs to  work out of the gate now of course after  that the rumors got shifted and the  reports and the parts that were designed  for this for example the iphone 14  and we had those reports for 2022 but  now it is scrapped and pushed back for  2023 meaning the iphone 15 and i just  have a really hard time believing that  they're going to wait that long and  still try to implement this i believe  that they wanted to make this work they  wanted to make it work earlier but at  this point they are so close to making  face id smaller for it to work better we  know that it's going to have the new  iphones are going to have hole punch  display so that whole tech is getting  miniaturized and the ultimate goal is to  be able to have it be underneath the  display and apple is also working on  that tech and i believe that that is  what's going to take over and then we  are not going to need this at all now i  do think that they still will have touch  id just not under the display technology  of course they still are going to have  budget ipads they have budget phones and  that is where having the fingerprint  sensor built into the power button makes  a whole lot of sense just like on the  ipad mini and the ipad air so hopefully  that tech will still be there and i kind  of wish that apple didn't just try to do  this on the display the hard way but  they just would have built into the  iphone's buttons um that would have been  really nice and convenient but of course  we know that they gave us the software  fix finally they could have done it a  while ago i believe but they didn't and  now since they did i believe they  decided to scrap that and just keep  moving forward with face id but you guys  let me know your thoughts down in the  comment section below i want to hear  your guys's opinions go ahead and click  that circle above to subscribe to help  us reach our goal of 1 million  subscribers and check out one of those  great videos right over there this has  been max and i'll see you in the next  video  [Music]

